  "findings": [
    "Opened all six actual PNGs. Fine parallel stripes on the foreground metal roof persist in baseline and receiveShadow=false at both bearings, and disappear when metal normalScale=0.",
    "Shadow-only treatment removes fixture shadows but preserves stripes. This supports corrugated tangent normal response as the artifact source, rather than PCF shadow acne.",
    "Pinned source normal has15 dominant U cycles per repeat; authored3m repeat gives0.20m physical ridge pitch. Existing material keeps weight0.155407539 at0.10m/pixel and residual0.018 beyond0.18m/pixel, allowing unresolved ridges to affect shading.",
    "Proposed fix fades actual normal-U footprint from8 to2pixels per measured ridge, reaches exactly zero at Nyquist, and retains existing full normal strength nearby. No texture removal, new maps/draws, source-UV changes or shadow suppression."
  ],
